 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Expense Report Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an expense report form?\", \"a\": \"An expense report form is the document an employee fills in to list business costs they paid. Each line gives a date, category, description and amount, backed by a receipt. The finished report goes to a manager for approval, then to finance for repayment and the books.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an expense report form?\", \"a\": \"Write down your spending caps and who approves first. Then describe them in one prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>, which builds the form, a table of every report, and the approval step. Employees then add lines with receipts and submit.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an expense reimbursement form?\", \"a\": \"An expense reimbursement form asks the company to pay an employee back for money spent on its behalf. An expense report can also record company card charges that need no repayment. A travel reimbursement form works the same way for the costs of one business trip. If you repay through payroll, the money goes to the account on the employee's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/direct-deposit-form'>direct deposit form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a sample expense reimbursement form include?\", \"a\": \"A good sample expense reimbursement form carries the business purpose and one line per expense with its receipt. Add an advance field if you issue cash up front, plus a sign-off from the approver. Purchases that need approval before any money is spent belong on a requisition form instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an employee reimbursement form?\", \"a\": \"An employee reimbursement form covers any out-of-pocket cost a staff member claims back, such as a client lunch or a certification exam. Keep it to an amount and a receipt for each claim. As claims grow, <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/accounts-payable-automation'>accounts payable automation</a> can batch approved claims into the next payment run.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a sample expense reimbursement form?\", \"a\": \"Accounting firms and template sites both publish free samples. The usual layout is a header for the employee over a grid of dated expenses. Compare a couple before you build. The fields they share are the ones an approver expects to find.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free expense reimbursement form template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Template sites post free ones, and Excel's template gallery includes expense report layouts. An expense report form in Excel is fine for a handful of reports a year. Emergent is free to start, and a form you build there saves each report as a row in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should an employee reimbursement form include receipts?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The receipt is how an approver checks the amount and how finance backs up the entry if it is ever questioned. Set one threshold in your policy and require a photo on every line above it. A line missing its receipt goes back to the employee, not on to the approver. Car trips are the exception: a mileage reimbursement form takes a log of miles driven in place of a receipt.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an employee reimbursement form be submitted online?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Staff fill it on a phone the day they spend the money, with a photo of the receipt on each line. Finance gets every claim as a record it can sort by employee or month, instead of a stack of emailed spreadsheets. Emergent puts no cap on how many claims the form takes in.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you automate an expense reimbursement form?\", \"a\": \"Automate the two handoffs that follow submission. The report goes to the employee's manager, who approves it or returns it with a note. Once approved, it posts to your accounting software through that tool's API. Every approver is included in an app built with Emergent, with no per-seat pricing.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
